# Technical Implementation — Kroll Pharmacy Automation PoC

This document explains **what technologies we use**, **what each one does**, and **how this repo implements them** so you can learn the stack end-to-end.

---

## 1. High-level architecture

Two **separate Python desktop processes** (not one monolithic app):

| Application | Path | Role |
|-------------|------|------|
| **Pharmacy Simulator** | `apps/pharmacy_simulator/` | Fake Kroll-style UI for pharmacists to click through manually |
| **Automation Controller** | `apps/automation_controller/` | External robot that drives the simulator via Windows UI Automation |

They communicate only through the **Windows desktop** (windows, controls, keyboard)—not HTTP or shared memory.

```text
┌─────────────────────────────┐     UIA / pywinauto      ┌──────────────────────────────┐
│  Pharmacy Simulator       │ ◄─────────────────────── │  Automation Controller       │
│  (PyQt6 GUI)              │   read/set by objectName │  (CLI: fill_save, enumerate) │
└─────────────┬─────────────┘                          └──────────────────────────────┘
              │
              ▼
       SQLite (database/pharmacy.db)
       JSON configs (config/)
       JSONL logs (logs/)
       Screenshots (screenshots/)
```

**Target workflow (PoC):**

```text
Inbox → OCR/Extract → Patient Search → Patient Record → Save
```

