## 2. Core language & runtime

### Python 3

- **What it is:** General-purpose language used for both the GUI app and automation scripts.
- **Why here:** Fast iteration, strong Windows desktop libraries, single `requirements.txt`.
- **How we use it:**
  - `apps/pharmacy_simulator/main.py` — starts the Qt event loop.
  - `apps/automation_controller/main.py` — CLI with `argparse` (`--connect-only`, `--enumerate`, `--workflow fill_save`).
  - Type hints (`str | None`, `Protocol`) for clearer interfaces.

### Standard library (no extra install)

| Module | Used for |
|--------|----------|
| `sqlite3` | Local database via repositories (`patient_repository.py`, `inbox_repository.py`) |
| `json` | Sample patients, inbox config, automation test patient, JSONL logs |
| `pathlib` | Project paths (`db_path.py`, `paths.py`) |
| `argparse` | Automation controller CLI |
| `re` | Regex extraction from fax/email text; date/combo helpers in UIA client |
| `dataclasses` | `ControlInfo`, extraction models |
| `typing.Protocol` | `IOCRProvider`, `IExtractionProvider`, `IKrollAdapter` — plug-in contracts |
| `uuid` | Generate patient IDs (`P-XXXXXXXX`) |
| `datetime` | Timestamps on save; validation (DOB not in future) |
| `ctypes` | `SetForegroundWindow` so automation clicks reach the simulator when the terminal has focus |

