## 6. Pharmacy simulator — implementation patterns

### 6.1 UI layer (PyQt6)

| Area | Location | Pattern |
|------|----------|---------|
| Main shell | `windows/main_window.py` | Menu, toolbar, opens Inbox / Search / Patient Record |
| Patient Record | `windows/patient_record.py` | Tabs + Save/Update + Randomize Layout |
| Inbox / Viewer / Search | `windows/inbox_window.py`, `document_viewer.py`, `patient_search.py` | Modal-style `QWidget` windows |
| Tabs | `tabs/general_tab.py`, `insurance_tab.py`, … | Form layouts + `objectName` on every widget |
| Dialogs | `dialogs/*.py` | Allergy search, family member, extraction review |
| Styling | `styles.py` | `QApplication` stylesheet — healthcare desktop look |

### 6.2 Accessibility contract (automation-facing)

- **Rule:** Every interactive control has stable `objectName` (e.g. `txt_first_name`, `btn_save`).
- **Helper:** `set_accessible(widget, "txt_phone")` sets `objectName` and `accessibleName`.
- **Why:** Automation never uses screen coordinates; it finds controls by name/AutomationId via UIA.
- **Dynamic layout:** `layout/dynamic_layout.py` shuffles visual order but **does not rename** controls (Module 9).

### 6.3 Validation

- `validation/patient_validator.py` — business rules (required last name, DOB format, phone, postal code, health card).
- Called before Save; focuses first invalid field by `objectName`.

### 6.4 Extraction pipeline (Strategy / Protocol pattern)

```text
Inbox document file
    → IOCRProvider.extract_text()  → OCRResult (raw text)
    → IExtractionProvider.extract_fields()  → dict (first_name, last_name, …)
    → ExtractionResult dialog → Patient Search prefill
```

| Piece | Implementation |
|-------|----------------|
| Interfaces | `extraction/interfaces.py` — `IOCRProvider`, `IExtractionProvider` |
| Working providers | `TextFileOCRProvider`, `RegexExtractionProvider` |
| Stubs | PDF/image OCR, OpenAI/Gemini — raise or return placeholders |
| Orchestrator | `DocumentProcessor` in `document_processor.py` |
| Models | `extraction/models.py` — `OCRResult`, `ExtractionResult` |

**Design intent:** Swap providers without changing UI code (same pattern planned for real OCR/LLM APIs).

### 6.5 Adapter stubs (future Kroll)

- `adapters/__init__.py` — `IKrollAdapter` Protocol (connect, save, search, set_field_value, …).
- `adapters/kroll_stubs.py` — `KrollUIAutomationAdapter` not implemented; points to `automation_controller` for real UIA today.

